# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AquaGuard AI — production frontend build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite loads `.env.production` automatically for `npm run build`, so a production
# build needs no extra flags:
#
#     npm run build
#
# This file contains PROJECT-LEVEL production defaults and is safe to commit,
# because every VITE_-prefixed value is compiled into the browser bundle and is
# therefore public. There are no secrets here and there must never be.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SINGLE-SERVICE MODE — the value below is RELATIVE on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo deploys the React app and the Flask API from ONE Render service:
# the build copies `frontend/dist` to `backend/app/static`, and Flask serves it
# from the same origin as `/api/*`. There is no second origin, so there is no
# CORS to configure and nothing to hard-code.
#
# `/api` is correct here. The bundle is served BY the API, so a relative path
# resolves against the same host and port automatically — including Render's
# preview URLs, where a baked absolute URL would point at production by mistake.
#
# DO NOT set an absolute `https://...onrender.com` URL here. That value is only
# right for the SPLIT layout (Netlify serves the UI, Render serves the API). In
# single-service mode it would make the browser call Render from Render — a
# needless extra round trip — and would break the moment the service is renamed.
#
# It must be:
#
#   * without a trailing slash;
#   * WITHOUT the `/api/v1` suffix. Every module in src/api/ appends its own path
#     (e.g. `/dashboard/overview`), and the backend's blueprints are mounted at
#     BOTH `/api/...` and `/api/v1/...`. So a base URL that already carries
#     `/api/v1` produces `/api/v1/api/v1/...` — which matches no route and
#     answers a bare 404. That is exactly the bug this line caused once; do not
#     put the version prefix back.
#   * listed in the backend's CORS_ORIGINS as the SITE origin, if and only if
#     the split layout is used. Single-service mode needs no entry at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_API_URL=/api

VITE_APP_NAME=AquaGuard AI
